1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:38,920
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,080
Let's sit there.

4
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:14,920
Excuse me.

5
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,360
Forget it.

6
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,080
Sit there.

7
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,280
Those foreigners keep looking at you.

8
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,040
I'm sure they'll chat you up real soon.

9
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:29,600
Come on.

10
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,480
You dressed so well today.
They're looking at you, not me.

11
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,040
Yes, look at me.

12
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,320
I can practice my English.

13
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,640
After all, we learn a foreign language
to travel the world.

14
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,120
Luke?

15
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,080
I see you made yourself comfortable.

16
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:52,360
We are doing Lime proud here.

17
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:54,120
We prove that Lime girls

18
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:56,960
are not just smart and capable,
but also beautiful.

19
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,280
Of course.

20
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,160
It's all thanks to your guidance.

21
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,280
Right, boss?

22
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,400
Stop it.

23
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,480
No need to flatter me
when we're on vacation.

24
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,760
Buy us a coconut, perhaps?

25
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,760
No.

26
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,360
‪No worries.

27
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,600
It's my treat. I'll buy some.

28
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,760
I'll come with you.

29
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:18,640
So stingy.

30
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,080
Hey, beauty.

31
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,680
Would you like some coconut juice?

32
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,600
My treat.

33
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:28,760
DO WE HAVE A FUTURE?

34
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:37,960
No need.

35
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,040
Thanks.

36
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:48,720
Lumi. Help me carry it.

37
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:56,880
What did I just tell you?

38
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,600
They are into you.

39
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,240
Come, boss.

40
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,080
Have a coconut.

41
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,040
No, thanks.

42
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,120
It's a treat from a handsome guy.
It's not right for me to take it.

43
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,760
Who cares? Just enjoy it. Here.

44
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:11,760
Try it. Here.

45
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,280
No, thanks.

46
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,480
You didn't get his number?

47
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,680
If we're meant to be,

48
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:20,920
we'll meet again.

49
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,560
Let's not just sit under the sun.

50
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:27,560
Should we go shopping?

51
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:28,480
Sure.

52
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,680
Boss, do you want to join us?

53
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,320
No.

54
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,960
Come with us.

55
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,880
- Why?
- To pay.

56
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:40,400
No girls who wear this
carry money with them.

57
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,920
Come.

58
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,920
Come.

59
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,560
Are we seriously spending his money?

60
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,480
Yes.

61
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,880
Now is the best time for him
to show off his generosity.

62
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,920
Splurge.

63
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:36,880
Eat anything you want.

64
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:39,400
Don't.

65
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,040
Look at this.

66
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,440
Do you want this one?

67
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,800
Come in.

68
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,960
People will see us if you do this.

69
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,160
Don't wear something like this again.

70
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:38,080
But I love it.

71
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,040
I want to wear it.

72
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,400
Do you do this to everyone?

73
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,480
Do what?

74
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,760
So controlling.

75
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,880
So possessive.

76
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:59,520
Others can wear or do whatever they want.

77
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,080
That's their freedom.

78
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,560
But not you.

79
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,920
I don't like it when men look at you.

80
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,040
Am I beautiful?

81
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,280
Yes.

82
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,200
Lethally beautiful.

83
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,840
Wait. Wait.

84
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,120
Someone's calling.

85
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:56,560
Hello?

86
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,240
<i>Flora. Are you free now?</i>

87
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,040
Yes. Why?

88
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,320
<i>Is something the matter?</i>

89
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,560
Nothing.

90
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:08,440
There's a bug here.

91
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,680
Go ahead.

92
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,600
<i>Come to the lobby bar.</i>

93
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,120
<i>I want to talk to you.</i>

94
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,240
Okay. I'm coming over now.

95
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,520
- Luan Nian.
- Who's that prick

96
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,680
who talks about work
during a team-building exercise?

97
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:23,800
Alex.

98
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:26,840
Why didn't you turn him down?

99
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,400
He's my boss.

100
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:33,760
I need his vote as well
for my promotion next month.

101
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:37,120
Before you forget, I can vote too.

102
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:53,960
I'm sure I can win it by myself.

103
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,520
Let's watch the sunrise
by the beach tomorrow.

104
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:58,960
Okay.

105
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:02,120
I have to work now.

106
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:11,000
<i>Luke.</i>

107
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,080
<i>Can we talk? It's an emergency.</i>

108
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:15,520
Hello?

109
00:10:16,560 --> 00:10:17,840
Alex is quitting.

110
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,640
- He is quitting?
- <i>Yes.</i>

111
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,520
<i>He just tendered his resignation.</i>

112
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:29,240
Perhaps you should reflect
on your oversight.

113
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,440
<i>Someone poached our manager,</i>

114
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:33,200
and you didn't even find out.

115
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,160
<i>I admit it is my fault.</i>

116
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,840
We are conducting an internal review
as we speak.

117
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,840
Don't worry. It won't happen again.

118
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,440
- Again?
- <i>Luke.</i>

119
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:43,440
Alex quit on us on such short notice.

120
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:45,000
You are rightfully annoyed.

121
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,280
But our priority now

122
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:49,000
is to minimize the impact
of Alex's resignation.

123
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,880
Where is he going?

124
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:53,840
Chuangyu.

125
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,920
An up-and-coming startup.

126
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,400
<i>I can suppress the news for now,</i>
<i>but not for long.</i>

127
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,240
He's leaving at the end of this month.

128
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,440
Okay.

129
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,680
Ask him to tie up the loose ends
of his projects

130
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:09,240
<i>and hand over everything properly.</i>

131
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,400
<i>In exchange,</i>

132
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,760
I will not hold him accountable
for his infringement.

133
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:14,360
Make sure to contain the rumors.

134
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,400
I do not want our employees to panic.

135
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,840
Understood. I'll talk to him
after you come back.

136
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:24,400
Also, pay attention
to Division One and Two.

137
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,120
Alex might poach some people as well.

138
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:30,240
Who do you think he'll poach?

139
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,320
Why me?

140
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,840
You've worked here
for quite some time, Flora.

141
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:41,000
I've seen what you can do.

142
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:42,360
Among the new recruits,

143
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:45,680
you progress the fastest
and have the biggest potential.

144
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:50,080
I love your learning speed and resilience.

145
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:54,000
Are you sure?

146
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,360
Lime has so many capable employees.

147
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,480
Besides,

148
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:01,000
I'm not even an account manager now.

149
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,080
I have not spearheaded any big projects.

150
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,760
How… How can I be helpful to you?

151
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,520
Why are you doubting yourself?

152
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,520
Are you questioning my judgment now?

153
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,960
- No.
- Come.

154
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,960
Let's go through what you've achieved
in the past two years.

155
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:21,280
You made Lime's supplier database.

156
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:25,280
You helped Lime close an important deal
with Yueteng Auto.

157
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:27,080
And you performed wonderfully
in last month's

158
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,760
automotive exhibition show.

159
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:31,360
Your resume is stellar.

160
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:34,400
If it weren't for Luan Nian's meddling,

161
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:36,280
you would have already become an AM.

162
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,720
Honestly, I feel bad for you.

163
00:12:45,120 --> 00:12:47,800
Join me in Chuangyu.

164
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:51,440
New company, new stage, new opportunity.

165
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:53,880
I'll give you the position of AM.

166
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,320
Your salary will be doubled,
and you will lead a team yourself.

167
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:00,200
No stupid rules to confine you.

168
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:03,080
You can just shine bright.

169
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:11,280
Alex, I do not intend
to switch jobs for now.

170
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,720
It's just so sudden.

171
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,240
I… I need time to think it over.

172
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,840
You can get back to me
after you think it through.

173
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:24,040
But keep this between us.

174
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,880
For our sake, as I'm sure you know.

175
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,760
Yes. Don't worry.

176
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,200
The opportunity waits for no one.

177
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:58,960
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

178
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,640
Thank you, everyone, for joining us.

179
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,800
Other than this trip, your special bonus

180
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,720
will be handed out together
with your salary next month.

181
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,440
Thank you.

182
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,680
- Thank you!
- Thanks, Luke.

183
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,320
Thanks, boss.

184
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,360
Flora.

185
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:26,400
Alex. Thank you.

186
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,280
Flora.

187
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,720
Alex.

188
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,800
I have to go now.

189
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,400
You talked to Alex?

190
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,160
Yes.

191
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,360
What did you two talk about?

192
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,960
Just work.

193
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:31,360
<i>Who do you think he'll poach?</i>

194
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,840
Flora.

195
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,320
Flora?

196
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:39,280
She was transferred from your team.

197
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:41,880
<i>I'm surprised she got along</i>
<i>with Alex this well.</i>

198
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:47,080
Her decision to leave with Alex or not
would be the litmus test of your charisma.

199
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:03,600
SHANG ZHITAO

200
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:04,800
<i>I'm here.</i>

201
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:51,320
Flora,

202
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,800
you've been working at Lime
for several years.

203
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,960
How do you feel?

204
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:59,160
<i>Aren't we supposed to watch the sunrise?</i>

205
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,640
<i>Why are we talking about work?</i>

206
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:06,160
I'm grateful for this opportunity

207
00:17:07,079 --> 00:17:12,319
and grateful that your strict guidance
has allowed me to grow rapidly.

208
00:17:14,839 --> 00:17:15,920
Grateful?

209
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,200
Is there nothing else you want to tell me?

210
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,080
No.

211
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:37,560
Luan Nian.

212
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:41,840
I'm happy that we get to watch
the sunrise together.

213
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,200
But I hope…

214
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:51,000
not just the sunrise.

215
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:54,040
I want to watch the sunset with you too.

216
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:57,640
Now, I'm done.

217
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,560
<i>The sunrise is so beautiful.</i>

218
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:41,840
<i>To watch the sunrise with him feels great.</i>

219
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:52,680
<i>Half of my feelings for him are love.</i>

220
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:56,600
<i>And the other half</i>
<i>is admiration and respect.</i>

221
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,400
<i>At this moment,</i>

222
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,480
<i>he's standing so close to me.</i>

223
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:12,400
<i>But this is something</i>
<i>I can't say out loud or hide.</i>

224
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:55,960
All right.

225
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,240
Let's call it a day.

226
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,520
Compile everything and send it to me
as soon as possible.

227
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:01,120
- Dismissed.
- I will double check.

228
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,680
- Okay.
- Sorry.

229
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,760
We'll only take up a few minutes.

230
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:07,240
We have an announcement to make.

231
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:14,040
Today is my last day at Lime.

232
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:22,880
I am grateful for your support
and understanding in my journey.

233
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:26,400
Before the new business manager arrives,

234
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:30,600
Luke will temporarily
take over Business Division Two.

235
00:20:33,600 --> 00:20:34,880
You have my blessings, Alex.

236
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:37,440
After I became the general manager,

237
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:39,840
I am grateful for your support

238
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,320
and the support
from the Customer Service Division.

239
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:45,200
You have led a formidable team.

240
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:47,600
I'll leave the floor to all of you.

241
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,880
I reserved a restaurant nearby
for Alex's farewell party.

242
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:59,440
Join us if you are free.

243
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:01,400
Thank you, Tracy.

244
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:02,880
All the best, Alex.

245
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:04,120
All the best, Alex.

246
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,720
I am honored

247
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,800
to have worked with all of you

248
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,720
all these years.

249
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,560
Don't sulk.

250
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:22,320
I'm just changing my job.

251
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,520
When you're free, hang out with me.

252
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:28,000
We can eat or drink.

253
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:29,840
Let's drink to your heart's content today.

254
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:30,760
- Okay.
- Okay.

255
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,480
- All right.
- Thanks, Alex.

256
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:33,800
Thanks, Alex.

257
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,480
See you at the restaurant.

258
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:37,960
Go back to your work.

259
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,000
- Hi, Alex.
- Alex.

260
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:50,920
A toast to you.

261
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:52,200
- A toast to you.
- Together.

262
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:53,160
Thank you.

263
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,680
May all go well in your next position.

264
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:55,920
Good luck.

265
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:00,760
Alex was doing so well.

266
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:02,160
Why did he leave?

267
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,520
To seek greener pastures.

268
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:08,720
There's a place better than Lime?

269
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:10,920
Will you work at Lime forever?

270
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:17,200
To him, the greener pastures
mean better pay,

271
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:19,280
bigger space, and more resources.

272
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:25,400
Then why didn't Lime
give him a counter-offer?

273
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,840
We did.

274
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:30,360
During the team-building exercise,

275
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:32,760
Luke talked to him. It didn't go well.

276
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,760
So be it then.

277
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:39,120
But to Luke,
Lime is never lacking in talent.

278
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:02,320
I was looking for you.

279
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:05,840
I know who Alex is taking with him.

280
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:07,800
Who?

281
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,720
Du Anni and Li Tianran.

282
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,720
Both of them are idiots.

283
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:15,000
Once they leave Lime,

284
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:18,280
they'll realize they owe
their stellar achievements

285
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,880
to this company.

286
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:26,160
Lumi, if it were you, would you leave?

287
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:29,520
Is this a joke? Why would I leave?

288
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,360
A new place means I have to adapt
to a new environment.

289
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:34,200
I'm comfortable in Lime.

290
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:36,400
I've adapted to this place. I own it.

291
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:37,680
People let me do what I want.

292
00:23:45,560 --> 00:23:49,040
Job-hopping has its pros and cons.

293
00:23:50,440 --> 00:23:53,240
If you leave with him,
you're forever his subordinate.

294
00:23:53,320 --> 00:23:55,280
If he succeeds, you'll be successful.

295
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:59,000
If he fails, you have to start all over.

296
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:03,480
But if you stay,
you have to face the new boss.

297
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:07,600
You don't know if you'll be sidelined.

298
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,400
But as long as you stay in Lime,

299
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:13,120
Luke will protect you.

300
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:16,760
Why?

301
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:19,680
Because Yueteng has retained us.

302
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,960
And you know them very well.

303
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,160
Right?

304
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:38,280
- Shall we grab a cab?
- My boyfriend is picking my up.

305
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:40,440
- Bye then.
- Bye.

306
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:41,560
Flora.

307
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,080
Alex.

308
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,600
You know I want you to come with me.

309
00:24:47,680 --> 00:24:49,480
On top of what I said last time,

310
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:51,800
there's also a personal reason.

311
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,880
I'll get back to you as soon as possible.

312
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:38,760
<i>If Alex wants you to go with him,</i>

313
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:40,240
<i>there can only be two reasons.</i>

314
00:25:40,320 --> 00:25:42,040
<i>You're cheap and obedient.</i>

315
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:51,600
<i>So even now, that's how he sees me.</i>

316
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:34,680
If you're leaving,
please tell me beforehand.

317
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:39,560
I'll talk to HR
and terminate your position.

318
00:26:39,640 --> 00:26:42,680
That way, you can get your severance pay.

319
00:26:45,840 --> 00:26:47,040
Thank you.

320
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:49,840
Once I have made up my mind,
I'll let you know beforehand.

321
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,840
So you truly are considering
taking up Alex's offer?

322
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:02,000
He gave you that offer
at Phuket, didn't he?

323
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:04,200
What did he tell you?

324
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:06,120
That you would be successful
if you followed him?

325
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:08,880
That your salary would double
and you would get promoted in a year?

326
00:27:14,160 --> 00:27:15,560
Shang Zhitao, do you have a brain?

327
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:18,760
Are you trying to fish out
an answer from me?

328
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:23,000
I wouldn't have to do this
if you didn't lie to me.

329
00:27:27,360 --> 00:27:29,400
I gave you a chance
just now and in Phuket.

330
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:31,520
But you chose to lie.

331
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:34,040
Are you that eager to leave with him?

332
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:37,320
You are not my direct superior.

333
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,120
I would be going over
my superior's head otherwise.

334
00:27:41,800 --> 00:27:44,280
If you want to talk about rules,

335
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,880
according to the company policy,

336
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:48,800
management-level employees
cannot poach any staff members

337
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,240
as it constitutes unfair competition.

338
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:52,840
You've signed the non-compete agreement.

339
00:27:53,560 --> 00:27:56,560
Since Alex loves to play dirty,

340
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:58,280
what do you think
our legal team will do to him?

341
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:16,440
Shang Zhitao, do you know
what your fundamental problem is?

342
00:28:17,920 --> 00:28:19,200
You do not have a firm principle.

343
00:28:20,120 --> 00:28:21,440
You are young.

344
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:23,440
How can you let small gains entice you?

345
00:28:23,520 --> 00:28:24,960
Have you thought about your future?

346
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:27,680
Or are you a shortsighted person

347
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:29,520
who only sees
the benefits in front of you?

348
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:32,200
Mr. Luan.

349
00:28:32,880 --> 00:28:33,920
My future?

350
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:36,680
If I want a future, I need money.

351
00:28:36,760 --> 00:28:38,640
I'm not like you.

352
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:40,120
You're used to your lofty palace.

353
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:42,640
That's why you can think
about your future.

354
00:28:42,720 --> 00:28:45,320
I came to Beijing alone
and rented a place with flatmates.

355
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:47,440
I am cheap and obedient.

356
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:49,400
It takes three hours
to travel to the office back and forth.

357
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:54,360
My happiness is decided by cheap things,
like my commute and wage.

358
00:28:54,440 --> 00:28:56,880
Alex told me that the new company
was close to my home.

359
00:28:56,960 --> 00:28:58,800
How can I not be enticed?

360
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:04,360
Will you even understand my situation?

361
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,800
Can you even empathize?

362
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,360
Besides, this is my private matter.

363
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,320
I don't need your intervention.

364
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:13,360
You think I want to care about you?

365
00:29:14,080 --> 00:29:16,400
I wouldn't have had to say all this
if you had used your brain once.

366
00:29:16,480 --> 00:29:18,480
Did I beg for your advice?

367
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:23,040
You want my answer, don't you?

368
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:25,280
Then, listen carefully.

369
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:28,120
I'm leaving with Alex. Why?

370
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:30,400
Because he supports me.
He talks to me nicely.

371
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:31,400
He respects me.

372
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:35,800
I wish you all the best.

373
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:36,800
I will do my best.

374
00:30:00,640 --> 00:30:02,760
<i>Not strong or firm enough.</i>

375
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:06,400
<i>Cheap. Obedient. Docile.</i>

376
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,840
<i>How can you let small gains entice you?</i>

377
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,280
<i>Have you thought about your future?</i>

378
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:12,920
<i>Or are you a shortsighted person</i>

379
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:14,680
<i>who only sees</i>
<i>the benefits in front of you?</i>

380
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:17,400
<i>Reckless. Didn't think it through. Eager.</i>

381
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:22,720
LUAN NIAN
IF ALEX WANTS YOU TO GO WITH HIM

382
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:24,160
THERE CAN ONLY BE TWO REASONS

383
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,600
YOU ARE CHEAP AND OBEDIENT

384
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:31,840
LUKE

385
00:30:35,040 --> 00:30:36,240
SETTINGS

386
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:37,480
BLOCK USER

387
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:38,520
BLOCK

388
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:39,680
BLOCKED

389
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:05,480
Why are you following me?

390
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,280
Were you abandoned too?

391
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:26,760
Dirty fella.

392
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:32,320
I'll help you find
your owner tomorrow, okay?

393
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:37,720
Come.

394
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:49,480
I love the renovation.

395
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:51,520
Very artsy.

396
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:53,480
How did you find the designer?

397
00:31:56,160 --> 00:31:58,040
The renovation fee must be…

398
00:32:00,040 --> 00:32:01,280
What's the matter?

399
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:03,760
Work or girls? Tell me.

400
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,280
Remember Alex?

401
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:10,000
Shang Zhitao is following Alex
to his new job.

402
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:11,680
And she lied to me.

403
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,120
I confronted her,

404
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:15,560
and she said she shouldn't go
over her superior's head.

405
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:22,360
In my eyes,

406
00:32:22,960 --> 00:32:25,880
Ms. Shang is more rational than you are.

407
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:27,960
You see.

408
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:30,400
If people mix work and private life,

409
00:32:30,480 --> 00:32:32,640
there will be no order.

410
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:35,200
Forget about the relationship.

411
00:32:35,280 --> 00:32:36,840
She is just your subordinate.

412
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:39,240
She can choose where she wants to work.

413
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:41,680
So I just watch her
as she makes the wrong decision?

414
00:32:44,160 --> 00:32:47,120
She's just young and reckless.

415
00:32:47,880 --> 00:32:49,440
She gets enticed by the smallest benefit.

416
00:32:49,960 --> 00:32:52,480
A job does not fall into your lap.

417
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:56,280
You sound like your father.

418
00:32:57,960 --> 00:33:00,480
Easy. Think positively.

419
00:33:01,600 --> 00:33:03,160
If she leaves Lime,

420
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:06,040
you no longer have to hide
your relationship anymore.

421
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:07,320
It's a good thing.

422
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:11,080
Luan Nian.

423
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:14,480
Ask yourself truthfully.

424
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:18,760
Are you worried that she'll leave Lime

425
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,360
or that she'll leave you?

426
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:27,160
Regardless of her choice,
I hope you can respect her.

427
00:33:27,800 --> 00:33:29,840
Because she is an independent person.

428
00:33:32,440 --> 00:33:34,000
If you don't want to lose her,

429
00:33:34,880 --> 00:33:36,040
win her back,

430
00:33:36,560 --> 00:33:39,280
and not just push her away
in a hurtful way.

431
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:01,920
STUDIO

432
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:10,520
Spent all 200,000 yuan your mom gave you?

433
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:17,800
I must say, it's a miracle
that the motley crew of yours

434
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:19,239
lasted three months.

435
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:24,000
Why?

436
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,360
Can't take a comment after you failed?

437
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:29,560
How can you start a business
when you're this sensitive?

438
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:32,840
Do you think business grows on trees?

439
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:35,120
How naive.

440
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:36,920
Starting a business
is not as simple as you think.

441
00:34:37,000 --> 00:34:38,040
The world outside is complicated.

442
00:34:38,960 --> 00:34:41,639
You refused to believe me
and took up a fool's errand.

443
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:45,199
So for a successful entrepreneur like you,

444
00:34:45,280 --> 00:34:48,040
you only judge people
by how much money they make?

445
00:34:50,120 --> 00:34:52,159
It is not the only standard,

446
00:34:52,239 --> 00:34:54,120
but it's the bare minimum.

447
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:56,239
Your company didn't make any money.

448
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:57,720
It was a net loss.

449
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:59,600
Who are you to judge my standard?

450
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:03,880
If nothing I do pleases you,

451
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:07,520
why did you lie that Mom was sick
and ask me to come back?

452
00:35:08,640 --> 00:35:10,440
Why are you two fighting again?

453
00:35:10,520 --> 00:35:12,720
Can't you talk properly?

454
00:35:14,880 --> 00:35:16,120
It's okay.

455
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:17,560
You don't have to worry about me anymore.

456
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:19,120
From now on, whether I live or die
has nothing to do with you.

457
00:35:19,200 --> 00:35:21,720
If you use my money, it is my business.

458
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:23,400
Hush already.

459
00:35:23,480 --> 00:35:24,320
Look at you.

460
00:35:24,400 --> 00:35:26,680
What do you have other than a box?

461
00:35:26,760 --> 00:35:27,760
Enough!

462
00:35:27,840 --> 00:35:29,160
It's not your money.

463
00:35:29,240 --> 00:35:30,440
Luan Nian did the right thing.

464
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:31,920
I support your decision.

465
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,480
You have my support.

466
00:35:33,560 --> 00:35:34,680
- Let's go back inside.
- Mom.

467
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:35,960
Two hundred thousand yuan.

468
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:38,160
I'll repay you together with the interest.

469
00:35:38,240 --> 00:35:39,760
Luan Nian. Luan Nian.

470
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:40,880
Luan Nian! You…

471
00:36:00,560 --> 00:36:02,440
STUDIO

472
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:11,160
<i>Are you worried that she'll leave Lime</i>
<i>or that she'll leave you?</i>

473
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,800
If you don't want to lose her,

474
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:15,680
win her back,

475
00:36:16,200 --> 00:36:19,200
and not just push her away
in a hurtful way.

476
00:36:19,280 --> 00:36:20,920
<i>Shang Zhitao, do you have a brain?</i>

477
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,120
<i>Have you thought about your future?</i>

478
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:23,720
<i>Or are you a shortsighted person?</i>

479
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:26,200
I'm leaving with Alex. Why?

480
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:28,400
Because he supports me.
He talks to me nicely.

481
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:29,320
He respects me.

482
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:43,640
<i>Sorry.</i>

483
00:36:43,720 --> 00:36:46,480
<i>The number you called cannot be reached.</i>

484
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:47,920
<i>Please try again later.</i>

485
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:58,200
SHANG ZHITAO, WHERE ARE YOU?

486
00:36:58,280 --> 00:36:59,120
THE USER HAS BLOCKED YOUR MESSAGE

487
00:37:09,600 --> 00:37:12,240
<i>Do you think business grows on trees?</i>

488
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:13,840
<i>How naive.</i>

489
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:15,040
<i>You took up a fool's errand.</i>

490
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:25,040
<i>How did I become</i>
<i>the person I hate the most?</i>

491
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:47,000
It's so solemn in here.

492
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:48,040
I almost thought

493
00:37:48,120 --> 00:37:49,560
Division Two were getting disbanded.

494
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,600
Report your work to me.

495
00:37:58,640 --> 00:37:59,480
Shang Zhitao.

496
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,760
You're doing the market analytics
for global new media.

497
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,200
How is the progress?

498
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:09,400
I have collected the necessary data

499
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:13,160
and will add domestic suppliers
into our media database.

500
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:18,560
Our rivals are posturing
to enter the new media market.

501
00:38:18,640 --> 00:38:20,280
We have to act quickly now.

502
00:38:20,920 --> 00:38:22,480
How long do you think you need?

503
00:38:24,040 --> 00:38:24,960
A month.

504
00:38:26,480 --> 00:38:29,560
If you can finish it in two weeks,
we'll have the edge.

505
00:38:30,560 --> 00:38:31,480
Can you do it?

506
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:39,240
Given that we are currently short-staffed,

507
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:42,640
I am unable to make that promise.

508
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:52,040
We'll stick to the same goal.

509
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:53,360
Two weeks.

510
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,080
I'll assign people
from other teams to assist you.

511
00:38:57,240 --> 00:38:58,080
Sit down.

512
00:39:13,040 --> 00:39:16,240
Flora, I can tell you have thought
carefully about your work.

513
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:20,760
Not only do you work hard,
you have a plan too.

514
00:39:21,840 --> 00:39:22,680
Keep it up.

515
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:34,880
Flora.

516
00:39:39,400 --> 00:39:40,360
You've changed.

517
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,400
You said no to Luke,

518
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:44,840
and somehow, he didn't rebut you.

519
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:45,960
He even praised you.

520
00:39:48,080 --> 00:39:50,840
I was just telling the truth.

521
00:39:53,240 --> 00:39:59,040
Did you tell him you couldn't make it
because you have decided to join Alex?

522
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:04,640
Let me tell you the truth.

523
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,840
I have not made the decision yet.

524
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:10,800
I said what I said in the meeting
because it truly is beyond my capability.

525
00:40:14,640 --> 00:40:15,640
Listen.

526
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:20,200
Personally, I don't want you to leave.

527
00:40:21,120 --> 00:40:26,000
Be it at work or hanging out as friends,
you are an amazing person.

528
00:40:26,080 --> 00:40:30,120
But you decide
if you want to stay or leave.

529
00:40:30,800 --> 00:40:34,040
You are so bright,
you'll shine wherever you go.

530
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:41,840
You truly think I… I'm very good?

531
00:40:41,920 --> 00:40:44,360
Yes. You're amazing.

532
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,880
Why else did Alex make you that offer?

533
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:53,000
I will respect your decision.

534
00:41:04,240 --> 00:41:05,960
WORK HARD IN OCTOBER AS WELL!

535
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,600
